165|     /** Get all the optima found during the last call to {@link
166|      * #optimize(UnivariateRealFunction, GoalType, double, double) optimize}.
167|      * <p>The optimizer stores all the optima found during a set of
168|      * restarts. The {@link #optimize(UnivariateRealFunction, GoalType,
169|      * double, double) optimize} method returns the best point only. This
170|      * method returns all the points found at the end of each starts,
171|      * including the best one already returned by the {@link
172|      * #optimize(UnivariateRealFunction, GoalType, double, double) optimize}
173|      * method.
174|      * </p>
175|      * <p>
176|      * The returned array as one element for each start as specified
177|      * in the constructor. It is ordered with the results from the
178|      * runs that did converge first, sorted from best to worst
179|      * objective value (i.e in ascending order if minimizing and in
180|      * descending order if maximizing), followed by Double.NaN elements
181|      * corresponding to the runs that did not converge. This means all
182|      * elements will be NaN if the {@link #optimize(UnivariateRealFunction,
183|      * GoalType, double, double) optimize} method did throw a {@link
184|      * ConvergenceException ConvergenceException}). This also means that
185|      * if the first element is not NaN, it is the best point found across
186|      * all starts.</p>
187|      * @return array containing the optima
188|      * @exception IllegalStateException if {@link #optimize(UnivariateRealFunction,
189|      * GoalType, double, double) optimize} has not been called
190|      * @see #getOptimaValues()
191|      */
192|     public double[] getOptima() throws IllegalStateException {
193|         if (optima == null) {
194|             throw MathRuntimeException.createIllegalStateException(LocalizedFormats.NO_OPTIMUM_COMPUTED_YET);
195|         }
196|         return optima.clone();
197|     }
